<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Serbian Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1813</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Serbian Uprising was the revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanjak-of-smederevo">Sanjak of Smederevo</a> against Ottoman rule from 1804 to 1813. Begun against the oppressive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> commanders, the dahijas, it grew under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadorde">Karađorđe Petrović</a> into a war for independence and set up a Serbian government; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> crushed it in 1813, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-serbian-uprising">Second Serbian Uprising</a> followed two years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-serbian-uprising.jpg" alt="First Serbian Uprising" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (Life time: 1811–1882) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osvajanje_Beograda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
